Subject: [PATCH] WindowManager: IME on the second screen keeps working with its own content

Ayaneo Pocket DS: the keyboard of apps on the main screen is shown on the second screen
(0001-ime-on-second-screen.patch). Since the second screen shows its own content (the
AYAHome launcher), the IME window lives on a display whose input target is another
window, so the show / hide requests of the main screen app never reached it
(PHASE_SERVER_ABORT_SHOW_IME_POST_LAYOUT, then PHASE_SERVER_SET_REMOTE_TARGET_IME_VISIBILITY).
When the IME target changes, the other display hosting the IME window takes the same
input target, and since that window is on another display, the shell (its remote insets
controller) controls the IME there; the app gets no IME insets for a keyboard that is
not on its screen.

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayContent.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayContent.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayContent.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayContent.java
@@ -5313,6 +5313,14 @@ class DisplayContent extends RootDisplayArea implements WindowManagerPolicy.Disp
         }
 
         final WindowState imeInputTargetWindow = mImeInputTarget.getWindowState();
+        // Ayaneo Pocket DS: the keyboard of the main screen is shown on the second screen
+        // (persist.sys.pocketds.ime_display). The display hosting the IME window takes the
+        // input target of the other display; the shell controls the IME there (the app does
+        // not get IME insets for a keyboard on another screen).
+        if (imeInputTargetWindow != null && imeInputTargetWindow.getDisplayContent() != this
+                && mRemoteInsetsControlTarget != null) {
+            return mRemoteInsetsControlTarget;
+        }
         if (!isImeControlledByApp() && mRemoteInsetsControlTarget != null
                 || getImeHost(imeInputTargetWindow) == mRemoteInsetsControlTarget) {
             return mRemoteInsetsControlTarget;
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowManagerService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowManagerService.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowManagerService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowManagerService.java
@@ -8674,6 +8674,19 @@ public class WindowManagerService extends IWindowManager.Stub
                             });
                         }
                     }
+
+                    // Ayaneo Pocket DS: the keyboard of the main screen can be shown on the
+                    // second screen (persist.sys.pocketds.ime_display). The display hosting it
+                    // takes the same IME input target, to get its show / hide requests, instead
+                    // of keeping its own (e.g. the second screen launcher), which would cancel
+                    // them: see DisplayContent#computeImeControlTarget.
+                    final int targetDisplayId = imeInputTarget.getDisplayContent().getDisplayId();
+                    mRoot.forAllDisplays(display -> {
+                        if (display.getDisplayId() != targetDisplayId
+                                && display.getImeWindow() != null) {
+                            display.updateImeInputAndControlTarget(imeInputTarget);
+                        }
+                    });
                 }
             }
         }
